Transients of the small-signal law families (R94's evidence owed): ../tran.py writes tran/ (step cap span/2000, 20 ps,
R84) and tran_fine/ (5 ps); ../tran_run.sh DIR runs both simulators (../../checked.sh, R91b: a run that did not
complete is refused; none was). Builds: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n,
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (vadng-pre-48). Each deck: the device on load.py's off-nominal cards (80 C, m=3,
geometry; junctions and Meyer or diffusion capacitances), gate (base) driven by a pulse through 10 kohm (a time constant
of a few ns against 1 ns edges, so the charges set the waveform), drain (collector) loaded by 2 kohm from 3 V. v(d) at
nine times, |ngspice - VACASK| / 3 V. mos1 and bjt_rbconst are the controls (no small-signal law).
vdmos_load (F30) is load.py's VDMOS card at 80 C, m=3, its gate through 10 ohm (cgs 1n: about 10 ns per copy), abstol
1e-12 as in vdmos_load/; vdmos_m1 the same at m=1 (control); vdmos_x3 three copies at m=1 in parallel, each with its
own thermal nodes: the m relation's oracle (m=3 must read as three copies, on each simulator against itself).
Result, MOS and BJT: no difference beyond step control. Worst |d|/3V per deck, cap 20 ps -> 5 ps:
  mos1 (control)   6.15e-05 -> 8.29e-06       mos2 2.09e-04 -> 2.64e-05      mos3 8.35e-05 -> 2.99e-05
  mos6             1.27e-04 -> 1.03e-05       mos9 1.76e-04 -> 2.99e-05
  bjt (irb)        2.69e-06 -> 2.67e-07       bjt_rbconst (control) 2.70e-06 -> 2.67e-07
Every difference sits on a switching edge and shrinks with the step (4x to 12x for a 4x smaller cap), as the
controls' do: the converged step uses the DC and charge laws, which agree; ngspice's Jacobian only steers Newton.
F27, F28, F29 do not reach transients.
Result, VDMOS: F30 reaches the transient. vdmos_load 2.68e-01 -> 2.69e-01 (t=30n: ngspice-45 2.4655 V, VACASK 3.2709 V),
not shrinking with the step; the controls agree: vdmos_m1 1.05e-04 -> 2.59e-04, vdmos_x3 3.79e-05 -> 1.52e-05.
The m relation accuses ngspice-45: its m=3 deck is not its own three copies (t=30n 2.465514 against 3.270829 V), while
VACASK's is (3.270941728 against 3.270942842 V). DC at m=3 agrees on both (vdmos_load/), so the difference is in the
charges or their time derivative at m != 1. Class: F30's point holds beyond linearised analyses (its carrier today
requires a linearised analysis or none).
Result, BSIM3v3 and BSIM4v8 (bsim3, bsim4, bsim4_nf: the corpus cards of ../cards/; the BSIM4 deck on a 1 V supply and
drive, so |d|/3V reads a third of its relative size): no difference beyond step control. Worst |d|/3V, 20 ps -> 5 ps:
  bsim3 1.08e-05 -> 8.59e-07    bsim4 3.08e-07 -> 7.85e-08    bsim4_nf 1.66e-06 -> 5.91e-08

